  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">One Health Companion Animal Program in Nauru 2023-2024 and 2024-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DFAT funds Darwin-based NGO Animal Management in Rural and Remote Indigenous Communities to lead a One Health / companion animal program in Nauru. This program consists of three to four visits annually to Nauru by veterinary science teams. Their primary focus is the provision of veterinary services to Nauruan dogs and cats (for which there is no domestic capacity) including surgery, desexing, medication, etc. They also provide education (including in schools) on dog safety, consult to the Government of Nauru, and undertake surveillance of zoonotic diseases.</narrative>
  </description>
